My two cents: Luke's quoted post below (especially the srana trick) is the
best solution if you don't want to be exact but do want to be truthful; I
was actually considering mentioning the srana idea before I read this post.

As for reasoning:
Allowing the universe of discourse, something that as of now cannot be
explicitly assigned easily (can you {zo'u} over multiple sentences
explicitly?) to simply fluctuate wildly with context is not a good standard
policy.
It's really, really easy to do.
It makes sense in general; you want to confine to pertinent things, so you
do. Done.

mu'o mi'e .latros.

